{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Getting the Job You Want", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Right Choices", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 9, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Third Conditional", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are four types of conditional sentences in English:<ol><li>Zero Conditional - to talk about certainty and facts</li><li>First Conditional - to talk about real possibilities in the present or the future</li><li>Second Conditional - to talk about <span class=\"italic\">unreal</span> possibilities in the present or the future</li><li>Third Conditional - to talk about unreal <span class=\"italic\">past</span> situations</li></ol>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the third conditional to talk about unreal situations in the past. <br/>These are things that did not happen in the past. You often use the third conditional to talk about regrets.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart below for the structure of the third conditional:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Conditional Name</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Structure</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Example</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Third \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> + Past Perfect, <span class=\\\"italic\\\">could</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">would have</span> + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If only I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had stayed</span> home that morning, I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would have gotten</span> the e-mail earlier.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "If only I had gotten his card the first time we met, yesterday's meeting wouldn't have been so awkward.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If I had his card, I could have called beforehand and not seemed quite so desperate. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If only I had stayed home that morning, I would have gotten the e-mail earlier.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If only I had talked to my source earlier in the week, I would have had a chance to apply. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If only I hadn't gone to the Corbin group in the morning, I would have had a chance at this opportunity. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Tag Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use<span class=\"italic\"> tag questions</span> to ask for clarification and confirmation.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Question tags</span> are short questions you can add to the end of a comment.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "They are mostly used in spoken English when you want to:<ul><li><span class=\"strong\">clarify/find out whether something is true or not true</span>, or</li><li><span class=\"strong\">to prompt a response</span> from the person we are speaking to.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ol><li value=\"1\">An <span class=\"strong\">affirmative</span> statement is followed by a <span class=\"strong\">negative</span> question tag.<br/> Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying 'yes' <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>You <span class=\"strong\">were</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">weren't you?</span></li> <li>You <span class=\"strong\">are</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> you?</li> <li>She <span class=\"strong\">has</span> a brother, <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> she?</li> <li>He <span class=\"strong\">can</span> speak English, <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> he?</li></ul></span></li></ol>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ol><li value=\"2\">A <span class=\"strong\">negative</span> statement is followed by an<span class=\"strong\">affirmative</span> question tag.<br/> Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying 'no'  <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>You <span class=\"strong\">weren't</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">were you? </span></li> <li>You <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">are</span> you?</li> <li>She <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> have a brother, <span class=\"strong\">does</span> she?</li> <li>He <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> speak English, <span class=\"strong\">can</span> he?</li></ul></span> </li></ol>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If the main verb is <span class=\"italic\">to be</span> or a <span class=\"strong\">modal verb</span>, the tag will be the same. <br/>For <span class=\"strong\">all other main verbs</span>, use the tag <span class=\"italic\">do</span>/<span class=\"italic\">does </span>or <span class=\"italic\">did</span>/<span class=\"italic\">didn't</span>. <br/>Look at the examples in the chart.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":11,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tag\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He is/was\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"isn't/wasn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"aren't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"can't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"couldn't we?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"won't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She has/had\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"doesn't/didn't she?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He likes\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"doesn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You like\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You liked\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"didn't you?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I talked about them previously, didn't I?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The position is still open, isn't it?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If I send my r\u00e9sum\u00e9 now I can still be considered, can't I?  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You aren't looking for anyone else, are you?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "beforehand", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in advance, earlier", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I could have called beforehand and not seemed quite so desperate.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear stories about regret.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "insight", "type": "name"}, {"content": "knowledge about something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He gave me some good insight into the organization.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "desperate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having an urgent need ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I could have called beforehand and not seemed quite so desperate.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "badgering", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to bother or annoy continuously ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I remember badgering the HR director with questions on the phone.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "awkward", "type": "name"}, {"content": "embarrassing or uncomfortable", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If only I had gotten his card the first time we met, yesterday's meeting wouldn't have been so awkward. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to scope out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to look at or over; examine", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I scoped out the Corbin group and talked to an employee there named Roger, who I actually knew. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I use the third conditional to express regret about the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present my regrets to a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a short essay about giving advice to my younger self.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my advice with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Imagine you have three regrets from your past you would like to change.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write sentences about your regrets using hypothetical situations in the past to explain your regrets in detail.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Then imagine you can give advice to your younger self. What would you say focusing on your three regrets?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Express your thoughts in 200 words.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your advice to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about emotions, opinions and behavior in a work situation. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about hypothetical situations in the past.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can ask for clarification and ask for someone's opinion. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "  Do you have any regrets? If so, what are they?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "  What do you wish you had tried or done when you were younger? Why?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Regrets. I have had a few!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "type": "WLC", "template_override": 1}, {"id": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "questions": [{"_d